3e the identity that actually explains the 10-task gap
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  scene      sends billed complt unbill |  sends billed complt
            learned arm                      | normal_immediate              
  2301901       11     10     10      0 |     11     11     11
  2301902       11     11     11      0 |     11     11     11
  2301903       11     11     11      0 |     11     11     11
  2301904       12      9      9      0 |     12     12     12
  2301905       11     11     11      0 |     11     11     11
  2301906       12      8      8      0 |     12     12     12
  2301907       11      8      8      0 |     11     11     11
  2301908       12     12     12      0 |     11     11     11

  completed set == billed set, learned arm   : True
  completed set == billed set, immediate     : True
  completions that were never billed         : 0 (both arms)
  duplicate sends  learned 11 / immediate 0

  This is the answer the separability question was reaching for, and it is not about
  feature quality. Every target that gets a first send completes on time; no target
  that is never billed ever completes. So the score IS the number of distinct targets
  the budget reaches, and a duplicate is a send that buys exactly nothing. The learned
  arm spent 11 of its 91 sends re-broadcasting a target already on the air, reached
  80 distinct targets against immediate's 90, and finished 10 tasks behind.
  No new feature fixes that: the same 19 dims already carry #2 sent_count and #12
  urgency; the policy simply did not condition on them, and the budget ran out first.

  Counterfactual, bounded by the same archive: if every duplicate had instead gone to
  a distinct target that was still detected by the last send step and still physically
  feasible there, the arm would have gained at most 4 tasks (80 -> 84), not 10.
  So dedupe alone explains at most half the gap; the other half is the order and the
  timing in which distinct targets were taken, which is exactly where a ranking
  feature could act.

